      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481422146": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Full Stack AI Developer | Python, React & Automation\nRemote – India or Pakistan | Full-Time\nSalary: $2,000 USD per month (flexible for exceptional talent)\nExperience: 3–5 years preferred | Ability matters more than years\nHelp us build an AI-powered recruitment company.\nAt We Are Revolution , we're building something ambitious: a recruitment business where AI, intelligent automation and great technology power almost everything we do.\nWe operate across the US and European recruitment markets, and we're investing heavily in technology to transform how our business works.\nOur goal is to automate entire workflows — from finding candidates and identifying opportunities to matching jobs, communicating with clients, managing recruitment pipelines and analysing performance.\nWe're looking for a talented Full Stack Developer who loves building things, solving problems and using AI to work faster and smarter.\nYou'll join a small, ambitious engineering team, working closely with our Head of Engineering to turn ideas into working products.\nThis isn't a role where you'll spend your days fixing tickets or making minor changes to somebody else's software.\nYou'll be building real systems, solving real business problems and seeing your work used every day.\nWhat you'll be building\nYou'll work across a variety of exciting projects, including:\nAI Agents: Building intelligent agents using Claude, OpenAI and other AI tools to automate complex business processes.\nFull Stack Applications: Developing internal platforms, dashboards and applications using React, Next.js, Python and FastAPI.\nBusiness Automation: Creating workflows using n8n, Python, APIs and AI to eliminate repetitive manual tasks.\nIntelligent Data Systems: Connecting and organising large volumes of candidate, client and recruitment data.\nSystem Integrations: Connecting Salesforce, recruitment CRMs, email platforms, calling systems and third-party APIs.\nAI-Powered Recruitment Tools: Developing systems that identify opportunities, match candidates to jobs and recommend the next best action.\nInfrastructure & Deployment: Deploying and maintaining reliable, scalable applications using modern cloud platforms.\nYou'll have the opportunity to work on projects from initial idea through to development, deployment and continuous improvement.\nThe skills we're looking for\nEssential:\nStrong experience with Python and JavaScript/TypeScript.\nExperience building full stack applications using React or Next.js.\nExperience developing APIs and backend services, ideally using FastAPI.\nGood understanding of databases, SQL and data structures.\nExperience integrating third-party APIs.\nExperience building automations using n8n, Python or similar tools.\nConfident using AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot.\nAbility to independently solve problems and deliver working software.\nNice to have:\nSupabase or Firebase.\nRender, Railway or similar deployment platforms.\nAI agents, MCP, LLM APIs or agent orchestration.\nSalesforce integrations.\nExperience building data pipelines or large-scale automation systems.\nYou don't need to know every technology listed. We're much more interested in someone who can learn quickly, solve problems and build great software.\nThe type of person who will thrive here\nWe're looking for a genuine builder.\nSomeone who enjoys taking a problem, understanding what needs to happen and figuring out the best way to make it work.\nYou'll probably enjoy this role if you:\nLove coding and building new products.\nAlready use AI tools to make yourself a more productive developer.\nEnjoy learning new technologies and experimenting with new ideas.\nTake ownership rather than waiting for detailed instructions.\nCan work across frontend, backend, databases and automation.\nCare about delivering working solutions, not just writing code.\nCommunicate clearly and enjoy being part of a collaborative team.\nWe value intelligence, curiosity, speed of learning and execution more than impressive CVs or academic qualifications.\nWhy join We Are Revolution?\nBuild with AI every day. You'll work with modern AI tools, automation platforms and emerging technologies on genuine commercial applications.\nWork on meaningful projects. Your software won't sit unused. You'll see the impact of what you build across a growing international business.\nReal responsibility and ownership. You'll be trusted to contribute ideas, make technical decisions and own projects.\nWork alongside experienced leadership. You'll collaborate directly with our Head of Engineering and company leadership, who are committed to investing in technology.\nOpportunity to grow. We're building an increasingly sophisticated technology platform, creating opportunities to develop your skills and responsibilities as the team grows.\nRemote working. Work from India or Pakistan as part of an international team.\nCompetitive compensation. We're looking for capability, not simply the cheapest developer. We'll consider stronger packages for exceptional candidates.\nHow to apply\nWe'd love to hear from you if you're a developer who genuinely enjoys building things and wants to work at the intersection of AI, software engineering and business automation .\nPlease send us your CV, GitHub or portfolio, and tell us briefly:\nWhat's the most interesting application, AI agent or automation you've personally built, and what did it achieve?\nWe care much more about what you've actually built than how many technologies you can list on your CV.\nCome and help us build the future of AI-powered recruitment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481445030": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the role:\nWe’re looking for a software engineer who is also interested in crypto markets and comfortable participating in day trading as part of the role.\nYou’ll work with us to research trading strategies, analyze market data, and build algorithms that can be tested and improved over time. A major part of the work will be studying 10 years or more of historical data where available , identifying patterns, testing hypotheses, and using evidence to evaluate trading ideas.\nThis is one integrated role: you’ll contribute to both the trading work and the software behind it. We’re open to students, recent graduates, and experienced candidates who can show strong technical and analytical skills alongside genuine crypto trading experience.\nWe value practical problem-solving. You should be comfortable finding useful exchanges, APIs, datasets, libraries, open-source projects, and existing tools, then connecting them into a working system. The goal is to build a stable crypto trading algorithm by assembling and improving what already works—not rebuilding every component from scratch.\nWhat you’ll do\nParticipate in crypto market research and day-trading activity.\nAnalyze long-term historical market data, including 10 years or more where reliable data is available.\nCollect, clean, validate, and analyze data from crypto exchanges and other relevant sources.\nUse data analysis and critical thinking to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and assess whether a strategy has evidence behind it.\nStudy price action, market behavior, and trading strategies, and help translate useful ideas into testable rules.\nDevelop Python tools and services for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nWork with exchange APIs, libraries, and other data sources; use scripting or automation where appropriate.\nResearch technical indicators and formulas using reliable references, open-source tools, and AI assistants such as Claude.\nVerify formulas and AI-generated code before using them in analysis or trading systems.\nConnect existing tools and services to fill gaps in the trading workflow.\nBuild and improve backtesting, monitoring, alerting, and execution components.\nTest strategies with historical data and simulated trading, then help evaluate live trading under defined risk limits.\nDocument your methods, assumptions, results, and limitations so the team can make data-informed decisions.\nWhat we’re looking for\nStrong interest in cryptocurrency markets and demonstrable experience buying, selling, or day trading crypto.\nComfort participating in day-trading research and activity as well as software development.\nStrong data analysis and critical analysis skills, with the ability to question assumptions and interpret results carefully.\nWorking knowledge of Python, including writing scripts for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nExperience using APIs, preferably exchange APIs, and handling structured data such as JSON.\nAbility to work with historical and time-series data and to evaluate trading ideas using evidence.\nFamiliarity with appropriate tools for data-driven analysis, such as pandas, NumPy, SQL, notebooks, statistical methods, or visualization tools.\nAbility to research indicators, understand the logic behind them, and translate ideas into code.\nA practical mindset: you look for suitable existing tools and libraries before building a replacement.\nGood communication skills and the ability to explain your reasoning, trading ideas, and technical decisions.\nCuriosity, discipline, and a willingness to learn from experiments that do not produce the expected result.\nHelpful experience\nFamiliarity with crypto exchanges, market-data feeds, order types, and trading dashboards.\nExperience analyzing large datasets, historical price data, or time-series data.\nExposure to backtesting, quantitative analysis, algorithmic trading, or risk management.\nExperience with tools such as Cursor, Claude, or other AI coding assistants.\nContributions to relevant open-source projects or personal trading, data analysis, or software projects.\nWho should apply\nYou do not need a particular degree or a long employment history. Students, recent graduates, self-taught developers, and experienced professionals are all welcome to apply if they can demonstrate relevant skills and trading experience.\nThis role combines hands-on crypto market participation with software engineering and data analysis. If you are interested only in coding and are not comfortable engaging with day-trading activity, this role may not be the right fit.\nHow to apply\nPlease include your résumé or LinkedIn profile.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481451013": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Introduction\nA career in IBM Consulting is built on long-term client relationships and close collaboration worldwide. You'll work with leading companies across industries, helping them shape their hybrid cloud and AI journeys. With support from our strategic partners, robust IBM technology, and Red Hat, you'll have the tools to drive meaningful change and accelerate client impact. At IBM Consulting, curiosity fuels success. You'll be encouraged to challenge the norm, explore new ideas, and create innovative solutions that deliver real results. Our culture of growth and empathy focuses on your long-term career development while valuing your unique skills and experiences.\nYour Role And Responsibilities\nAs an Application Developer specializing in SAP ABAP HANA, you will design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on the HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP). You will work on designing, developing, and re-engineering highly complex application components, integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nYour Primary Responsibilities Will Include\nDevelop Application Solutions: Design, develop, and support application solutions with a focus on HANA version of ABAP, ensuring seamless integration with existing systems and platforms.\nIntegrate Software Packages: Integrate software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms, leveraging knowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture.\nRe-engineer Application Components: Re-engineer highly complex application components to optimize performance, scalability, and reliability, utilizing ABAP Development Tools (ADT) and Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA.\nModel Data using HANA Studio: Create data models using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nConsume HANA Live Models: Consume HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nRequired Technical And Professional Expertise\nExposure to SAP ABAP HANA: Experience working with HANA version of Advanced Business Application Programming (ABAP), including designing, developing, and supporting application solutions.\nKnowledge of SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture: Familiarity with SAP HANA Technical Concept and Architecture, including data modeling using HANA Studio and ABAP Development Tools (ADT).\nExperience with Data Modeling: Exposure to data modeling using HANA Studio, adhering to best practices and ensuring data consistency and integrity.\nUnderstanding of Code Performance Rules: Familiarity with Code Performance Rules and Guidelines for SAP HANA, including ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nIntegration Experience: Experience integrating software packages, programs, and reusable objects residing on multiple platforms.\nPreferred Technical And Professional Experience\nWorking Knowledge of HANA Live: Familiarity with consuming HANA Live models to deliver real-time insights and analytics, leveraging knowledge of ADBC, Native SQL, and ABAP Core Data Services.\nExposure to Database Procedures: Understanding of database procedures, text search, and ALV on HANA, including data base procedures and HANA Live models consumption.\nFamiliarity with ABAP Core Data Services: Knowledge of ABAP Core Data Services, including data modeling and code performance optimization techniques.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481852097": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Join the G2i Talent Pool\nWe’re always meeting great people in tech. Join the G2i Talent Pool and let us get to know you.\nG2i works with top AI labs and fast-growing companies. Our community of engineers works on real projects, from evals and RL environments to training data for frontier models.\nWho We’re Looking For\nSoftware, data, AI/ML, infrastructure, security, design, QA and product. Experienced or just starting out, fresh graduates are welcome. If you work in tech or are building your career in it, we’d love to meet you.\nHow It Works\nApply in a few minutes with your real details and links.\nWe review your profile and send you a short technical assessment.\nOnce you pass, you join our pool and hear from us when a project fits your skills.\nJoining the pool doesn’t mean immediate work, since matching depends on what our clients need and on each profile. But we’re always working to match everyone in our pool with the right project.\nPlease note that eligibility may vary depending on your location, as some regions may not be supported by the client.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482203207": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Goldschmitt and Associates LLC (G&A), we’re not just another company—we’re a catalyst for innovation and impact, and we’re inviting passionate, forward-thinking individuals to join us on this journey. Recognized multiple times on the Inc 5000 list of the fastest-growing companies, G&A is a leader in tech transformation and system modernization for some of the nation’s most important federal agencies.\nOur culture is built on creativity and collaboration. We offer flexible schedules, telework options, and an environment where your ideas truly matter. At G&A, you won’t just clock in—you’ll be solving real-world challenges and working on projects that make a difference in the lives of millions.\nJoining our team means becoming part of a vibrant, connected community where innovation thrives, your voice is heard, and your impact is felt. Whether you’re a tech enthusiast, a strategic thinker, or a problem-solver, at G&A, you’ll have the opportunity to level up your career while making a real-world impact.\nIf you’re ready to be part of a company that values purpose as much as progress, G&A is the place for you!\nSummary:\nGoldschmitt is seeking a Frontend Developer.\nThis position is remote with preference given to candidates who live within a commutable distance to the DMV area.\nThe anticipated salary for this position is $85,000.00- $115,000.00, dependent upon experience.\nThe anticipated travel for this position is 5%.\nJob Duties and Responsibilities:\nDesign, develop, and maintain responsive, user-friendly web application interfaces, dashboards, and reports\nTranslate software requirements and business processes into functional user interfaces\nDevelop and execute functional UI tests and automated tests\nTroubleshoot, debug, and optimize frontend functionality and performance\nCollaborate with backend developers, testers, and other team members to deliver high-quality software\nParticipate in code reviews and maintain established development standards\nNecessary Skills and Knowledge:\nExperience developing and maintaining enterprise web applications\nMinimum Qualifications:\nPossess at least 3 years of professional frontend software development experience\nPossess a Bachelor's degree\nPossess the ability to pass and maintain eligibility for a Public Trust investigation, including United States citizenship\nPossess experience with the following:\nJavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, CSS3/SCSS, React (hooks, function components) and Redux / Redux Toolkit, Node.js\nDevelopment of data-heavy pages with pagination, tables, custom sorting/filtering, complex forms with validation, and modals\nDevelopment of CRUD operations against RESTful APIs, including async state management\nClient-side routing (React Router) and role-based routes\nPreferred Qualifications:\nPossess experience developing scheduling, workforce management, or government applications\nPossess experience with the following:\nVitest or Jest with React Testing Library; API mocking with MSW\nExperience developing interactive dashboards, data visualizations, and reporting interfaces within web applications.\nPrint-optimized layouts and PDF report generation\nBootstrap 5 / React-Bootstrap\nAWS services: Cognito, CloudWatch, AWS GovCloud\nTypeScript",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483635899": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nParsons is a digitally enabled solutions provider with nearly 75 years of experience, specializing in defense, security, and infrastructure markets. We deliver cutting-edge cyber and converged security solutions, technology-based intellectual property, and innovative services to federal, regional, and local government agencies, as well as private industrial customers worldwide. Our Federal Solutions segment supports critical missions globally by providing resources and expertise in defense, intelligence, infrastructure, and environmental sectors. We foster a culture of excellence, innovation, and collaboration, empowering our employees to contribute to impactful projects that protect and sustain our nation’s most vital assets.\nAbout The Role\nParsons is seeking a talented Front End Software Engineer to join our dynamic team. In this role, you will be responsible for developing and maintaining frontend software applications using JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js. You will work closely with cross-functional teams in an Agile/Scrum environment to enhance application usability and user experience. Your contributions will include designing, testing, debugging, and delivering high-quality software. Additionally, you will participate in pair programming, peer reviews, and sprint planning sessions, while supporting automated testing and troubleshooting production issues. This position offers the opportunity to work remotely with occasional travel and requires an active Secret security clearance.\nQualifications\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent experience (minimum 5 years)\nActive Secret security clearance (mandatory)\nProficiency in JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js\nExperience with Git and modern version control workflows\nStrong background in developing and maintaining frontend applications\nExperience working in Agile/Scrum development environments\nExcellent collaboration skills including pair programming and peer reviews\nStrong troubleshooting, problem-solving, and communication skills\nDesired qualifications include experience with:\nAutomated end-to-end testing frameworks such as Cypress\nJest, React Testing Library, unit and integration testing\nMaterial UI or similar frontend component libraries\nCI/CD pipelines and DevSecOps practices\nContainerization and orchestration tools like Docker and Kubernetes\nCloud platforms such as AWS, Platform One, or DAF CLOUDworks\nBackend technologies including Java, Spring Boot, Node.js, or Python\nData technologies such as PostgreSQL, Liquibase, SPARQL, Elasticsearch, or Logstash\nSecurity concepts including OAuth, JWT, OWASP principles, secure coding, CVEs, and penetration testing\nExperience using Jira for issue tracking and management\nSupporting government, Air Force, COMSEC, CCI, or cryptographic systems\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and maintain frontend software applications using JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js\nImplement enhancements to improve application usability and user experience\nDesign, develop, test, debug, and maintain software throughout the development lifecycle\nCollaborate with engineers and cross-functional teams in an Agile/Scrum environment\nParticipate in pair programming, peer reviews, backlog refinement, and sprint planning\nInvestigate and resolve software defects and troubleshoot production issues\nContribute to automated frontend testing development and maintenance\nSupport software release quality and related testing activities\nDocument software, processes, and technical solutions as appropriate\nWork effectively as part of a fully remote team with occasional travel requirements\nBenefits\nCompetitive salary range of $103,500 to $181,100\nComprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance\nPaid time off and holidays to support work-life balance\n401(k) retirement savings plan\nLife insurance coverage\nFlexible work schedules\nOpportunities for professional growth and career advancement\nSupportive and inclusive work environment\nEqual Opportunity\nParsons is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status. We are committed to fostering diversity and inclusion in the workplace and encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484040948": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\nWe are looking for a highly skilled Java Developer with strong experience in Spring Boot and Microservices architecture. The ideal candidate will design, develop, and maintain scalable backend services in a cloud-native environment.\nKey Result Areas\n• Design and develop RESTful APIs using Java 8/11/17\n• Build microservices using Spring Boot\n• Implement service-to-service communication (REST, Kafka, etc.)\n• Work with relational and NoSQL databases\n• Write clean, testable, production-grade code\n• Participate in architecture discussions and technical design\n• Implement security using JWT/OAuth2\n• Optimize application performance and scalability\n• Follow CI/CD and DevOps practices\n• Troubleshoot production issues and perform root cause analysis\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n• Strong experience in Java & OOP concepts\n• Hands-on experience with Spring Boot\n• Experience building Microservices architecture\n• Experience with REST APIs\n• Database experience (SQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MongoDB)\n• Understanding of Docker & Kubernetes\nExperience with Git\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484280001": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nWorking at Atlassian\nAtlassians can choose where they work – whether in an office, from home, or a combination of the two. That way, Atlassians have more control over supporting their family, personal goals, and other priorities. We can hire people in any country where we have a legal entity.\nTo help our teams work together effectively, this role is fully remote, but requires you to be located in either US Pacific or Mountain time zones .\nYour future team\nWe're hiring a Front End Software Engineer, reporting to an Engineering Manager. Here, you'll work closely with design and product management, influencing the direction of the product and collaborating with team to get there. You'll write code and ship product capabilities that you are proud of and delivering amazing results that our customers love and help us become the best project management tool for business teams!\nResponsibilities\nResponsibilities\nDeliver projects autonomously, from technical design to launch\nBuild client code that is efficient, fast, testable, scalable, and high quality.\nPromote collaboration with other engineers, designers and managers to understand user pain points and iterate to deliver solutions\nPartner with design and product and across other engineering teams to develop delightful customer experiences\nContribute to code reviews and documentation, and take on complex bug fixes\nCompensation\nAt Atlassian, we strive to design equitable, explainable, and competitive compensation programs. We follow consistent hiring practices and account for each candidate's skills, knowledge, and experience when setting base pay within the range.\nPlease visit go.atlassian.com/payzones for more information on which locations are included in each of our geographic pay zones. However, please confirm the zone for your specific location with your recruiter.\nThis role may also be eligible for benefits, bonuses, commissions, and equity.\nPay Ranges\nRole\nIn The United States , we have three geographic pay zones. For this role, our current base pay ranges for new hires in each zone are:\nZone A : $150,300 - $196,225\nZone B : $135,270 - $176,603\nZone C : $124,749 - $162,867\nQualifications\nQualifications\n2+ years of experience building large-scale frontend applications using React.\nBachelor's degree with a preference for Computer Science degree\nUnderstanding of modern frontend ecosystem, including but not limited to bundling, linting, testing and releasing.\nExperience with modern testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, Cypress, Mocha, Chai)\nFamiliarity of the JavaScript language and ecosystem\nExperience building frontend applications at scale\nExperience in Agile software development methodologies\nExperience engineering software systems of medium-to-large scope and complexity\nBenefits & Perks\nAtlassian offers a wide range of perks and benefits designed to support you, your family and to help you engage with your local community. Our offerings include health and wellbeing resources, paid volunteer days, and so much more. To learn more, visit go.atlassian.com/perksandbenefits .\nAbout Atlassian\nAt Atlassian, we're motivated by a common goal: to unleash the potential of every team. Our software products help teams all over the planet and our solutions are designed for all types of work. Team collaboration through our tools makes what may be impossible alone, possible together.\nWe believe that the unique contributions of all Atlassians create our success. To ensure that our products and culture continue to incorporate everyone's perspectives and experience, we never discriminate based on race, religion, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, or marital, veteran, or disability status. All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines.\nTo provide you the best experience, we can support with accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process. Simply inform our Recruitment team during your conversation with them.\nTo learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit go.atlassian.com/crh .\nIn line with local law, identity verification (which may include use of biometric data) is a condition of employment with Atlassian for employment fraud purposes.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484442793": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Division\nJonas Premier Construction - a division of Constellation Software Inc. – is the market-leading cloud-based integrated construction management solution, for mid-sized General Contractors, Design Builders and Land Developers. Constellation companies are leading developers of technology solutions for vertical markets in North America, Europe and Australia. Jonas Software is the valued technology partner of over 8000 customers worldwide in 15 countries. Jonas is headquartered in Canada and also operates offices in the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Caribbean.\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Lahore resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of .NET programming\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nStrong relational database concepts with SQL queries.\nGood level of knowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meet deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, AngularJS/Angular.\nGood communication skills in English.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-10-29T10:06:23.811314+00:00"
  },
